# booping — /groom-playbook

**Experimental.** Playbook-driven grooming, running in parallel to `/groom`. Same outcome — a specified, estimated, user-approved plan — but the procedure comes from the core `groom` playbook instead of this skill body. `/groom` remains the canonical entry point.

{% include "_partials/_project_context.j2" %}

The playbook is `groom`. It requires an attached booping project — if none is attached (see Project Context above), tell the user to run `/install` and stop.

Pass `$ARGUMENTS` (the task description or issue reference) into the first wave's step as the request under grooming.

{% include "_partials/_playbook_driving.j2" %}
## Completion report

After the last step, give a one-paragraph summary: the plan file written, its status, and the gates passed.

Cross-session resume is not yet supported — a run lives entirely within one conversation. The playbook's own preamble carries the in-vault resume mapping for re-entering an unfinished plan.

